        "80d3ee7d-e860-4a9c-8b84-2c5508cdf136": {
          "type": "entry",
          "settings": {
            "full_width_enable": true,
            "title": "Maintenance",
            "text": "<p><strong>Cleaning the Pre-Filter</strong><br/><br/>1) Remove the dust bin.<br/>2) Press the dust bin lid release button, and open the lid.<br/>3) Clean pre-filter by gently tapping over a waste bin.<br/>4) Reinstall the dust bin into the main body.<br/><br/>NOTE: It is recommended to clean the pre-filter every three months to optimise performance.<br/><br/><strong>Cleaning the Pre-Motor Filters</strong><br/><br/>1) Remove the dust bin.<br/>2) Remove the foam and felt filters.<br/>3) Wash with cold water only. Do not use detergent or soap. Squeeze by hand and allow to air dry before reinstalling. Do not operate without foam and felt filters installed. Do not wash in the dishwasher. Do not install foam and felt filters if damp.<br/>4) Replace felt and foam filters into the vacuum cleaner.<br/>5) Reinstall the dust bin.<br/><br/>NOTE: We recommended cleaning the foam and felt filters with cold water every three months.<br/><br/><br/><strong>Cleaning the HEPA Exhaust Filter</strong><br/><br/>1) Remove the exhaust filter cover by pulling the tab outward at the bottom of the cover.<br/>2) Press the release tab and remove the exhaust filter from vacuum cleaner.<br/>3) Wash with cold water only. DO NOT use detergent or soap. Allow to air dry. Allow parts to dry 24 hours before putting back into vacuum cleaner. DO NOT wash in the dishwasher. DO NOT install the filter if damp.<br/>4) Reinstall the exhaust filter into the vacuum cleaner until a click is heard.<br/>5) Insert the exhaust filter cover tabs into the upper slots and lock the exhaust filter cover into place by pressing the lower part of the cover until a click is heard.<br/><br/><strong>Removing hair from the WrapFree™ Brushroll</strong><br/><br/>If you see any hair wrapped around the brushroll, continue cleaning, ensuring the On/Off switch is in 'II' position with the brushroll rotating on low pile carpets or tile floors. Hair will be removed from the WrapFree<strong>™</strong> brushroll and be sucked into the dust bin.<br/></p>",
            "button_1_style": "",
            "button_1_text": "",
            "button_1_url": "",
            "button_2_style": "",
            "button_2_text": "",
            "button_2_url": "",
